        "gemma": "`? Yes.\n\n    *Self-Correction:* \"Recall\" can sometimes mean \"remember\", but in a technical \"agentTools\" context, it almost certainly means \"retrieve from database\". \"Recuperar\" is the correct term.\n\n    Final choice: \"No se pudieron recuperar las conversaciones anteriores.\" or \"Error al recuperar las conversaciones anteriores.\"\n    Usually, \"Failed to...\" is translated as \"No se pudo...\" or \"Error al...\".\n    \"No se pudieron recuperar las conversaciones anteriores\" is slightly more polite/formal.\n\n    Let's try: \"No se pudieron recuperar las conversaciones anteriores.\"\n\n    Wait, \"recall\" in the context of an AI agent often refers to \"recalling\" information.\n    \"No se pudieron recuperar las conversaciones pasadas.\"\n\n    Let's go with: \"No se pudieron recuperar las conversaciones anteriores.\"\n\n    Actually, \"Error al recuperar las conversaciones anteriores\" is more concise and standard for a key path like `recallConversations.error`.\n\n    Let's check the \"polite-formal\" requirement.\n    \"No se pudieron recuperar las conversaciones anteriores\" is a complete sentence and feels more polite than a fragment.\n\n    Final check:\n    Source: \"Failed to recall past conversations.\"\n    Spanish: \"No se pudieron recuperar las conversaciones anteriores.\"\n\n    Wait, \"past conversations\" -> \"conversaciones pasadas\" is also correct. \"Anteriores\" is slightly more formal.\n\n    Let's use: \"No se pudieron recuperar las conversaciones anteriores.\"<T>No se pudieron recuperar las conversaciones anteriores.",
